it is going to do.\n\nNothing should happen automatically without the user's knowledge.\n\n---\n\n## User Control\n\nAutomatic analysis only creates suggestions.\n\nThe final Launch Profile always belongs to the user.\n\nUsers should be able to completely customize every launch action.\n\n---\n\n## Simplicity\n\nDevLauncher should solve one problem extremely well:\n\nLaunching development environments.\n\nFeatures unrelated to this goal should not be added unless they directly improve the launch experience.\n\n---\n\n## Cross Platform\n\nDevLauncher is designed to work on Windows, Linux, and macOS.\n\nDevelopment begins on Windows.\n\nPlatform-specific logic should always remain isolated to make future ports straightforward.\n\n---\n\n## Local First\n\nEverything belongs to the user.\n\nLaunch Profiles and application settings are stored locally as JSON files.\n\nNo cloud.\n\nNo accounts.\n\nNo synchronization.\n\nNo telemetry by default.\n\n---\n\n# Internal Architecture\n\nThe application consists of several independent subsystems.\n\n## Project Analyzer\n\nAnalyzes a project folder.\n\nDetects technologies, project structure, and launchable components.\n\nProduces a suggested Launch Profile.\n\nIt never launches anything.\n\n---\n\n## Launch Profile Manager\n\nStores and edits Launch Profiles.\n\nResponsible for saving and loading project launch configurations.\n\n---\n\n## Launch Engine\n\nExecutes Launch Profiles.\n\nRuns actions in the correct order.\n\nHandles failures.\n\nNever analyzes projects.\n\n---\n\n## Process Monitor\n\nTracks running processes.\n\nProvides status information.\n\nDetects crashes.\n\nAllows restarting individual processes.\n\n---\n\n## System Integrations\n\nCommunicates with the operating system.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Open VS Code\n* Launch applications\n* Open browser\n* Start processes\n* Read filesystem\n* Detect installed software\n\nPlatform-specific code belongs here.\n\n---\n\n## Settings\n\nStores global application settings.\n\nExamples:\n\n* VS Code path\n* Browser path\n* Terminal\n* Theme\n* Preferred applications\n\nStored in JSON.\n\n---\n\n## UI\n\nDisplays information.\n\nNever contains business logic.\n\nThe UI communicates with the backend through Tauri commands.\n\n---\n\n# Core Entity\n\nThe central concept of DevLauncher is the **Launch Action**.\n\nEverything the application does is represented as an action.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Run Command\n* Open Application\n* Open URL\n* Wait for URL\n* Wait for Port\n* Delay\n* Execute Script\n\nA Launch Profile is simply an ordered collection of Launch Actions.\n\n---\n\n# Technology Stack\n\nDesktop Framework:\n\n* Tauri v2\n\nFrontend:\n\n* Svelte\n* TypeScript\n* Vite\n\nBackend:\n\n* Rust\n\nPersistence:\n\n* JSON files\n\nThe frontend is responsible only for the user interface.\n\nThe Rust backend contains all business logic, filesystem access, process management, and operating system interactions.\n\n---\n\n# AI Development Guidelines\n\nWhen assisting with this project:\n\n* Do not redesign the architecture unless explicitly requested.\n* Prefer extending existing systems over introducing new abstractions.\n* Keep components loosely coupled.\n* Avoid unnecessary complexity.\n* Explain engineering decisions, not only implementation.\n* Prefer maintainability over cleverness.\n* Every feature should move the application toward becoming a reliable daily developer tool.\n\nWhen writing code:\n\n* Produce small, understandable iterations.\n* Explain why each architectural decision is made.\n* Keep code modular and testable.\n* Follow existing project conventions instead of inventing new patterns.\n\nThe objective is not only to build DevLauncher, but also to help the developer understand the engineering decisions behind it.. и вот, у меня есть сейчас в этом проекте базовая структура созданная svelte, vite и и tauri, а также я попробовал и смог создать одну рабочую кнопку (ping rust). теперь я хочу уже начать делать свой проект. но я вообщ