ements the `Manager` trait. The `path()` method returns a `PathResolver` in Tauri v2.\n\nHmm, actually I'm not 100% sure about the exact API. Let me just write it in a way that will work. If it doesn't compile, we'll fix it.\n\nIn Tauri v2, the typical pattern for getting app data dir in setup:\n\n```rust\nuse tauri::Manager;\n\n.setup(|app| {\n    let data_dir = app.path().app_data_dir()?;\n    // ...\n    Ok(())\n})\n```\n\nI believe `app.path()` works through the `Manager` trait. Let me proceed with this.\n\nOne more consideration: the `ActionStatus` enum. I defined it in `launch_engine.rs`. But it should probably be in `models.rs` since it's a return type that the frontend might need to deserialize. Actually, for the skeleton, launching won't be implemented yet, so I'll keep it in the engine module.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. In the skeleton:\n- `models.rs` has the core data types (LaunchAction, LaunchProfile, ActionType)\n- Module files have their traits and implementations\n- Each module can have its own internal types\n\n`ActionStatus` is a return type that the frontend will need to deserialize. So it should probably be in `models.rs` or have its own serde derives. Let me put it in `models.rs` to keep things simple.\n\nOK let me now write everything.\n\nWait, I also need to handle the `launch_engine.rs`'s `execute_action` return type. The Tauri command `execute_action` returns `Result<ActionStatus, String>`. But `ActionStatus` needs Serialize. Let me add it to models.\n\nActually I'll add it to models.rs. Let me finalize the plan:\n\n### Files to create/modify:\n1. `src-tauri/src/models.rs` - update with comments + ActionStatus\n2. `src-tauri/src/profile_manager.rs` - new file with trait + JsonProfileManager\n3. `src-tauri/src/launch_engine.rs` - new file with trait + SimpleLaunchEngine\n4. `src-tauri/src/analyzer.rs` - new file with trait + SimpleAnalyzer\n5. `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` - new file with all Tauri commands\n6. `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` - update to wire everything\n7. `src/lib/types.ts` - new file with TypeScript types\n8. `src/lib/api.ts` - new file with typed API functions\n9. `src/routes/+page.svelte` - update to use the new API\n\nLet me write them all. I'll create all the files in one go, then verify.\n\nActually, `src/lib/` directory might not exist. Let me check what `src/` contains...\n\nFrom earlier: `src/` contains `app.html` and `routes/`. No `lib/` directory. I'll create it.\n\nLet me also think about the `$lib` alias. In SvelteKit, `$lib` maps to `src/lib/` by default. So `$lib/types` and `$lib/api` will work.\n\nOK let me proceed to write all the files now.\n\nOne thing I want to make sure: the `ProfileManager::list_profiles()` should return the profiles sorted or something. For the skeleton, it's fine to return them in whatever order they're read from disk.\n\nAlso, for `JsonProfileManager`, I need to think about how to name the files. I'll use the profile name as the filename: `{name}.json`. But I need to sanitize the name for the filesystem. For the skeleton, I'll just use the name as-is and note that in production it should be sanitized.\n\nLet me write the code now.\n\nFor the `profile_manager.rs`:\n\n```rust\n//! Управление профилями запуска.\n//!\n//! # Архитектура\n//!\n//! `ProfileManager` — это трейт (интерфейс), описывающий\n//! операции с профилями. Любая реализация этого трейта\n//! может быть подставлена в приложение.\n//!\n//! `JsonProfileManager` — конкретная реализация, хранящая\n//! профили как JSON-файлы в指定нной директории.\n\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::fs;\nuse crate::models::*;\n\n/// Интерфейс для управления профилями запуска.\n///\n/// Send + Sync — требуется Tauri для безопасной работы\n/// с состоянием из разных потоков.\npub trait ProfileManager: Send + Sync {\n    /// Возвращает список всех профилей.\n    fn list_profiles(&self) -> Result<Vec<LaunchProfile>, String>;\n    \n    /// Возвращает профиль по имени.\n    fn get_profile(&self, name: &str) -> Result<LaunchProfile, String>;\n    \n    /// Сохраняет профиль (создаёт или перезаписывает).\n    fn save_profile(&self, profile: &LaunchProfile) -> Result<(), String>;\n    \n    /// Удаляет профиль по имени.\n    fn delete_profile(&self, name: &str) -> Result<(), String>;\n}\n\n/// Реализация ProfileManager, хранящая профили в JSON-файлах.\npub struct JsonProfileManager {\n    /// Путь к директории с JSON-файлами профилей.\n    profiles_dir: PathBuf,\n}\n\nimpl JsonProfileManager {\n    pub fn new(profiles_dir: PathBuf) -> Self {\n        Self { profiles_dir }\n    }\n\n    /// Вспомогательный метод: путь к файлу профиля по имени.\n    fn profile_path(&self, name: &str) -> PathBuf {\n        self.profiles_dir.join(format!(\"{}.json\", name))\n    }\n}\n\nimpl ProfileManager for JsonProfileManager {\n    fn list_profiles(&self) -> Result<Vec<LaunchProfile>, String> {\n        let mut profiles = Vec::new();\n        let entries = fs::read_dir(&self.profiles_dir)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read profiles directory: {}\", e))?;\n\n        for entry in entries {\n            let entry = entry.map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read entry: {}\", e))?;\n            let path = entry.path();\n            if path.extension().map_or(false, |ext| ext == \"json\") {\n                let content = fs::read_to_string(&path)\n                    .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read {}: {}\", path.display(), e))?;\n                let profile: LaunchProfile = serde_json::from_str(&content)\n                    .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to parse {}: {}\", path.display(), e))?;\n                profiles.push(profile);\n            }\n        }\n\n        Ok(profiles)\n    }\n\n    fn get_profile(&self, name: &str) -> Result<LaunchProfile, String> {\n        let path = self.profile_path(name);\n        let content = fs::read_to_string(&path)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read profile '{}': {}\", name, e))?;\n        serde_json::from_str(&content)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to parse profile '{}': {}\", name, e))\n    }\n\n    fn save_profile(&self, profile: &LaunchProfile) -> Result<(), String> {\n        let path = self.profile_path(&profile.name);\n        let content = serde_json::to_string_pretty(profile)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to serialize profile: {}\", e))?;\n        fs::write(&path, content)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to write profile '{}': {}\", profile.name, e))\n    }\n\n    fn delete_profile(&self, name: &str) -> Result<(), String> {\n        let path = self.profile_path(name);\n        fs::remove_file(&path)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to delete profile '{}': {}\", name, e))\n    }\n}\n```\n\nFor the `launch_engine.rs`:\n\n```rust\n//! Движок запуска профилей.\n//!\n//! LaunchEngine выполняет действия из LaunchProfile одно за другим.\n//! Он не анализирует проекты — только исполняет.\n\nuse crate::models::*;\n\n/// Трейт для движка запуска.\n///\n/// Каждая реализация должна уметь выполнить одно действие.\npub trait LaunchEngine: Send + Sync {\n    fn execute_action(&self, action: &LaunchAction) -> Result<ActionStatus, String>;\n}\n\n/// Простейшая реализация LaunchEngine.\n///\n/// Пока просто логирует действие и возвращает Success.\n/// В будущем здесь будет запуск процессов, открытие URL и т.д.\npub struct SimpleLaunchEngine;\n\nimpl LaunchEngine for SimpleLaunchEngine {\n    fn execute_action(&self, action: &LaunchAction) -> Result<ActionStatus, String> {\n        if !action.enabled {\n            return Ok(ActionStatus::Skipped {\n                reason: format!(\"Action '{}' is disabled\", action.label),\n            });\n        }\n\n        match &action.action_type {\n            ActionType::RunCommand { command, working_dir } => {\n                println!(\"[LaunchEngine] Would run: '{}' in {:?}\", command, working_dir);\n                Ok(ActionStatus::Success {\n                    message: format!(\"Command queued: {}\", command),\n                })\n            }\n            ActionType::OpenUrl { url } => {\n                println!(\"[LaunchEngine] Would open URL: {}\", url);\n                Ok(ActionStatus::Success {\n                    message: format!(\"Opening URL: {}\", url),\n                })\n            }\n            ActionType::Delay { seconds } => {\n                println!(\"[LaunchEngine] Would wait: {}s\", seconds);\n                Ok(ActionStatus::Success {\n                    message: format!(\"Delayed {}s\", seconds),\n                })\n            }\n            _ => Ok(ActionStatus::Success {\n                message: format!(\"Simulated: {}\", action.label),\n            }),\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait, I should add `ActionStatus::Skipped` to the enum. Let me add it to models.\n\nActually, let me think about this. The `ActionStatus` types are:\n- `Success { message }`\n- `Failed { error }`\n- `Skipped { reason }` (when action is disabled)\n\nLet me add this.\n\nFor the `analyzer.rs`:\n\n```rust\n//! Анализатор проектов.\n//!\n//! ProjectAnalyzer изучает структуру папки проекта\n//! и предлагает LaunchProfile с предполагаемыми действиями.\n//! Анализатор никогда не запускает действия.\n\nuse crate::models::*;\n\n/// Трейт для анализатора проектов.\npub trait ProjectAnalyzer: Send + Sync {\n    fn analyze(&self, project_path: &str) -> Result<LaunchProfile, String>;\n}\n\n/// Заглушка анализатора.\n///\n/// Просто возвращает пример профиля.\n/// В будущем будет анализировать package.json, docker-compose.yml и т.д.\npub struct SimpleAnalyzer;\n\nimpl ProjectAnalyzer for SimpleAnalyzer {\n    fn analyze(&self, _project_path: &str) -> Result<LaunchProfile, String> {\n        // TODO: имплементировать анализ проекта\n        Ok(LaunchProfile {\n            name: \"analyzed project\".into(),\n            description: format!(\"Auto-detected profile for {}\", _project_path),\n            project_path: Some(_project_path.to_st