ould be the most logical and useful. It would:\n1. Take a LaunchProfile\n2. Execute actions in order\n3. Handle failures (stop on failure or continue)\n4. Return execution status for each action\n5. Support cancellation\n\nThis is a natural extension of the LaunchEngine. The user can build a `ProfileRunner` module that orchestrates the LaunchEngine.\n\nBut the user said \"более широкий модуль\" (broader module). Let me think about what's truly useful and teachable.\n\nActually, I think a good next module would be:\n- **Process Monitor** - A system to track running processes, provide status, allow restart/kill\n- This is more complex and interesting than just running a profile\n- It has real architectural challenges (cross-process communication, async tracking)\n- It's a critical part of the manifest (mentioned explicitly)\n\nLet me write the instructions for this.\n\nKey points to cover:\n1. What the module should do\n2. What files to create/modify\n3. What APIs to use\n4. How it connects to existing systems\n5. Design considerations\n\nLet me keep it concise but clear.",
